{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Iterations 0–2 results\nAt 1000 paths and 28 prompts/asset/window, configuration CRPS (COM_EQU_24H / CRYPTO_24H / CRYPTO_1H current-rule replay):\n- Starter: Aug1 3307.6917 / 2831.1013 / 629.1511; Aug2 2204.8470 / 6688.7651 / 1215.7233.\n- Constant five-minute calibration: Aug1 3294.5858 / 2825.8628 / 630.5776. Most equity benefit is not explained by resampling alone.\n- Seasonal: Aug1 3070.0857 / 2794.0311 / 631.9575; Aug2 2021.6821 / 6641.9823 / 1209.4321.\n- Adaptive: Aug1 3063.4947 / 2784.7846 / 626.6187; Aug2 2022.8387 / 6598.9684 / 1199.1483.\n- Adaptive scale .85: Aug1 3018.3364 / 2751.8141 / 618.1878; Aug2 2017.2154 / 6620.7537 / 1187.7614.\n- Adaptive mixture .4: Aug1 3027.3906 / 2763.2964 / 624.1603; Aug2 2012.2900 / 6578.8981 / 1193.8057.\nVerdict: keep seasonality, retain robust-scale and mixture candidates; reject universally faster adaptation and universal .85 scale as settled conclusions. Narrowing helps quiet conditions but loses some crypto24h advantage in the busy window. Rank unused.\nLesson: improvement must survive volatility regime changes. Coverage identical across variants (99.762% Aug1, 99.357% Aug2); residual holes limit absolute score interpretation.\n\n## Iteration 4 — session resolution (pre-registered)\nHypothesis: coarse hourly variance profiles blur the US cash open at 13:30 UTC. Robust absolute-return profiles and 30/15-minute bins may better model session transitions.\nChange: freeze June–July profiles using squared returns or absolute returns; compare 24, 48, 96 daily bins with the same weekday pooling. Pair with the absolute EWMA estimator; no regression artifact trained under a different normalization is reused.\nKill threshold: retain finer profiles only when both windows improve or the gain is consistent across assets and exceeds 0.5%; otherwise prefer fewer parameters.\nResult / Verdict: pending.\nEOF\ncp agent/run_grid.py agent/run_seasons.py\nuv run python - <<'PY'\np='agent/run_seasons.py';s=open(p).read();a=s.index('variants={');b=s.index('\\\\nfor window',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''variants={\n'abs24':{'MODEL_MODE':'absolute','SEASON_FILE':'seasonality_abs24.json'},\n'abs48':{'MODEL_MODE':'absolute','SEASON_FILE':'seasonality_abs48.json'},\n'abs96':{'MODEL_MODE':'absolute','SEASON_FILE':'seasonality_abs96.json'},\n'var48':{'MODEL_MODE':'absolute','SEASON_FILE':'seasonality_var48.json'},\n'var96':{'MODEL_MODE':'absolute','SEASON_FILE':'seasonality_var96.json'},\n}'''+s[b:];open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nuv run agent/run_seasons.py > agent/seasons.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > agent/fit_mean.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"A deliberately regularized drift test; training ends before validation.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom predict import load_lenient,ensure_workspace_cwd\nensure_workspace_cwd()\nseason=json.loads(Path('agent/seasonality.json').read_text());models={};metrics=[]\nfor step in [60,300]:\n for asset in season['tables']:\n  if step==60 and asset not in ['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE']:continue\n  df=load_lenient(asset,pd.Timestamp('2026-06-01',tz='UTC'),pd.Timestamp('2026-07-31 23:59',tz='UTC'))\n  log=np.log(df.close.resample(f'{step}s').last());r=log.diff()\n  scale=r.abs().rolling(86400//step,min_periods=300//step).mean()*np.sqrt(np.pi/2)\n  horizon=3600//step if step==60 else 86400//step\n  feats={str(h):(log-log.shift(int(h*3600/step)))/(scale*np.sqrt(h*3600/step)) for h in [.25,1,6,24,72]}\n  x=pd.DataFrame(feats).clip(-4,4)\n  y=(log.shift(-horizon)-log)/(scale*np.sqrt(horizon))\n  rows=x.copy();rows['y']=y;rows=rows.iloc[72*3600//step:-horizon:3600//step].dropna()\n  X=rows.iloc[:,:-1].to_numpy();Y=rows.y.clip(-5,5).to_numpy()\n  # No intercept: drift must be supported by signed recent-return features.\n  beta=np.linalg.solve(X.T@X+np.eye(X.shape[1])*1000,X.T@Y)\n  pred=X@beta\n  models[f'{asset}_{step}']=beta.tolist()\n  metrics.append(dict(asset=asset,step=step,n=len(rows),fit_r2=1-float(np.mean((Y-pred)**2)/np.mean(Y**2))))\nPath('agent/mean.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(fit_end='2026-07-31',models=models),indent=2))\nprint(pd.DataFrame(metrics).to_string(index=False))\nPY\nOPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 uv run agent/fit_mean.py > agent/mean_fit.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
