{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_120","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/suggestions.md <<'EOF'\n- Follow-up diagnosis: a historical-score response exceeded its requested end boundary and tripped the defensive assertion before saving or using those scores. No out-of-range score values were inspected or used for model selection. Recovery now ends requests a day earlier (September 13) and explicitly discards every unsolicited row outside the requested range before any analysis. Treat API date bounds as requiring client-side enforcement.\nEOF\nuv run agent/cache_scores.py > agent/cache_scores_retry.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_121","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Iterations 9–10 results\nEmpirical innovations and five-step blocks fail to beat the HAR Gaussian mixture across both windows. For example, empirical+mixture crypto1h is 619.0742 / 1190.4479 versus Gaussian mixture 618.4267 / 1183.8016. Five-step blocks reduce the empirical regression but do not reverse it. COM changes are small and inconsistent between windows. Verdict: discard empirical and block resampling as universal replacements. The Gaussian scale mixture is both simpler and better calibrated in these tests.\n\n## Iteration 11 — independent August confirmation and seed stability (pre-registered)\nHypothesis: the gains from seasonal HAR survive a previously unused interval and denser prompts, while tiny dependence/shape gains may be sampling noise.\nChange: freeze four finalists: original HAR mixture0.4, robust half-hour HAR mixture0.4, half-hour HAR with scale0.9, and half-hour HAR with fitted MA(1). Evaluate August 8–16 at 3h cadence. Separately repeat half-hour HAR and its MA(1) variant on original August windows with seeds 123 and 987. These runs use 1000 paths.\nKill threshold: discard scale/dependence modifications if gains reverse in the new interval or are not consistent across seeds. Select at most one broadly supported configuration-specific combination before opening September confirmation.\nResult / Verdict: pending.\nEOF\ncat > agent/run_confirm.py <<'PY'\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport os,subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\njobs=[]\nvariants={\n'har_orig':{'MODEL_MODE':'har','MODEL_MIX':'.4'},\n'har48':{'MODEL_MODE':'har','MODEL_MIX':'.4','SEASON_FILE':'seasonality_abs48.json','HAR_FILE':'har_abs48.json'},\n'har48_09':{'MODEL_MODE':'har','MODEL_MIX':'.4','MODEL_SCALE':'.9','SEASON_FILE':'seasonality_abs48.json','HAR_FILE':'har_abs48.json'},\n'har48_ma':{'MODEL_MODE':'har','MODEL_MIX':'.4','MODEL_DEPENDENCE':'fitted','SEASON_FILE':'seasonality_abs48.json','HAR_FILE':'har_abs48.json'},\n}\nfor name,env in variants.items():jobs.append((name+'_augmid','2026-08-08','2026-08-17',3,env))\nfor seed in ['123','987']:\n for window,start,end in [('aug1','2026-08-01','2026-08-08'),('aug2','2026-08-17','2026-08-24')]:\n  for name in ['har48','har48_ma']:\n   jobs.append((name+'_'+window+'_s'+seed,start,end,6,{**variants[name],'SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED':seed}))\ndef run(job):\n tag,start,end,hours,extra=job\n if 'LANDING ORDER' in Path('agent/BUDGET.md').read_text():return tag,'landing'\n env=os.environ.copy();env.update(extra);env['OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS']='1';env['OMP_NUM_THREADS']='1'\n with open('agent/results_'+tag+'.log','w') as log:\n  p=subprocess.run(['uv','run','agent/predict.py','--research','--model','agent/modeling.py','--tag',tag,'--start',start,'--end',end,'--hours',str(hours)],env=env,stdout=log,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)\n return tag,p.returncode\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=3) as pool:\n for result in pool.map(run,jobs):print(result,flush=True)\nPY\nuv run agent/run_confirm.py > agent/confirm.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_122","type":"agent_message","text":"The nonlinear model and empirical-return resampling did not beat the simpler mixture consistently, so they’re being discarded. The finalists are now running on an unused August interval and with additional seeds. I also found that the score API can return rows outside the requested dates; the cache loader now discards those rows before analysis and requests dates ending a day earlier."}}
