{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_170","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nSeptember robustness failure: the first HAR runs stopped at AAPLX because a short feature window contained no observed return. Fixed feature construction by substituting the longer observed return scale for missing short-window summaries (with a pre-cutoff fitted prior only when no return scale exists). No missing price is filled or interpolated. Re-running the failed candidate evaluations; the starter had completed successfully. This is a contract fix, not score-based parameter tuning.\nEOF\nMODEL_MODE=har MODEL_MIX=.4 SEASON_FILE=seasonality_abs48.json HAR_FILE=har_abs48.json OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 uv run python - <<'PY'\nimport sys,os\nsys.path.insert(0,'agent')\nimport numpy as np,pandas as pd\nfrom predict import load_lenient\nfrom modeling import simulate\nx=load_lenient('AAPLX',pd.Timestamp('2026-09-01',tz='UTC'),pd.Timestamp('2026-09-07 23:57',tz='UTC'))\nfor label,frame in [('last hour missing',x.copy()),('single observed close',x.copy())]:\n if label=='last hour missing':frame.iloc[-60:,:]=np.nan\n else:\n  last=frame.close.dropna().iloc[-1];frame.iloc[:,:]=np.nan;frame.iloc[-1,frame.columns.get_loc('close')]=last\n a=np.array(simulate('AAPLX','2026-09-08T00:00:00Z',300,86400,17,frame)[2:])\n assert a.shape==(17,289) and np.isfinite(a).all() and (a>0).all()\n assert (a[:,0]==frame.close.dropna().iloc[-1]).all()\n print('PASS',label)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
